    "body": "## Purpose\n\nA sliding-window KV group keeps one null block per out-of-window block, so a long request's block table is almost all null (8,183 of 8,192 entries for a 128K-token prompt with a 128-token window and 16-token blocks). `KVCacheBlocks.get_unhashed_block_ids_all_groups` and `SingleTypeKVCacheManager.free` walked every entry in Python. This PR skips that null head.\n\n* `null_head_len()` finds the leading null run by binary search and checks it with one `list.count` of the shared null block. If the null blocks are not one contiguous head, it falls back to a scan.\n* `get_unhashed_block_ids_all_groups` and `pop_blocks_for_free` (so both `free` and the deferred-free path) start after the head. `free_blocks` skips any other null blocks; the null block's `ref_cnt` is not maintained (see `BlockPool.__init__`).\n* No behavior change: the same block ids are collected, and the same blocks reach the free queue in the same order.\n\nNot a duplicate: I searched open PRs for `null block sliding window free`, `null_block free_blocks`, `sliding window null blocks` and `get_unhashed_block_ids`. vllm-project/vllm#42276 and #55818 change SWA eviction and allocation, not these walks.\n\n## Where it matters\n\nThe cost is paid per sliding-window group, on the scheduler's critical path, each time a request is admitted with async KV loads or freed. It shows up when GPU steps are short and requests turn over quickly, as in **DeepSeek V4.1 Flash, WideEP DEP16 decode** (GB300, 64 requests/rank, 169.5K-token prompts):\n\n* A decode step takes ~22 ms on the GPU, and all 16 DP ranks wait for the slowest rank's scheduler.\n* Each rank admits and frees ~9 long requests per second.\n* Each request has 8 sliding-window groups x 5,298 blocks, 5,292 of them null.\n\n| Scheduler CPU per request | main | PR |\n| -- | --: | --: |\n| free | 2.0 ms | 0.5 ms |\n| async-KV admission (135K prompt) | 0.73 ms | 0.47 ms |\n\nEnd to end, output throughput went from 8,892 to 9,025 tok/s/GPU **(+1.5%).** \n\n## Microbenchmark\n\nOne request on one sliding-window group (window 128, block size 16): `KVCacheBlocks.get_unhashed_block_ids_all_groups` (collect) and `SlidingWindowManager.free` (free). Median of 300 calls on a Grace CPU, main (`8530aed2b7`) vs this PR, consistent across two runs.\n\n| Prompt tokens | Blocks (null) | Collect, main / PR (us) | Free, main / PR (us) |\n| -- | -- | --: | --: |\n| 32K | 2,048 (2,039) | 54.1 / 9.7 | 92.9 / 10.8 |\n| 128K | 8,192 (8,183) | 214.9 / 34.8 | 370.6 / 35.8 |\n| 512K | 32,768 (32,759) | 867.5 / 135.9 | 1471.7 / 137.5 |\n\n## Test Plan\n\n```bash\npytest tests/v1/core/test_kv_cache_utils.py tests/v1/core/test_single_type_kv_cache_manager.py tests/v1/core/test_prefix_caching.py -q\npre-commit run --files <changed files>\n```\n\nNew test `test_null_head_len`: empty, no-null, all-null, contiguous-head and non-contiguous tables, plus `get_unhashed_block_ids_all_groups` on two groups.\n\n## Test Result\n\n312 passed. Pre-commit (ruff, format, typos, mypy) passes.\n\n---\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used to write and benchmark this change.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
